{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest","id":1168734,"title":"are the scions the strongest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-19T00:41:31-08:00","id":1168734,"title":"are the scions the strongest?","content":"I was thinking while reading vampire &quot; fuck... low generation vampire are so fucking strong...&quot; then i realized that an apollo or ra (sun gods) can beat the shit out Cain with legend 4 with just a flash of light. <br /> <br /> This is bad.<br /> <br /> So, basically a moon god's scion is able to destroy a werewolf with silvery weapon<br /> <br /> A mage have nothing to do with a full dex-strenght scion that will bring him down in a sec<br /> <br /> So... scions are the strongest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T00:49:16-08:00","id":1168737,"title":"","content":"Why does this matter? Scions don't even exist in Vampire: the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T00:51:05-08:00","id":1168739,"title":"","content":"just for the fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T01:06:40-08:00","id":1168740,"title":"","content":"Scions are literal children of Gods. Makes sense to me that they'd be tougher than Vampire or Werewolf PCs.<br /> <br /> Now granted I'm not really a WoD fan so I can't really speak for some of the higher-end stuff.<br /> <br /> Though I do like the image of many high-ranked Vampires trying to hold a meeting to plan for what to do... And it's interrupted by a group of Death God Scions. Turns out their parents are rather annoyed that these undead have gone uncollected for so long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T01:57:09-08:00","id":1168745,"title":"","content":"We're also using games with radically different assumptions on how some key system elements work. Unless you want to put in the work to fairly replicate WoD characters in Scion, and comparison - even just for fun - is biased in the Scions favor before even getting to when Scions start to outpace high powered WoD critters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:17:36-08:00","id":1168761,"title":"","content":"Next you'll be worrying about whether Scions are stronger than bards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T07:30:13-08:00","id":1168793,"title":"","content":"All of this is immaterial of course because we know Hulk is strongest there is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:44:27-08:00","id":1168822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest#post1168734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking while reading vampire &quot; fuck... low generation vampire are so fucking strong...&quot; then i realized that an apollo or ra (sun gods) can beat the shit out Cain with legend 4 with just a flash of light.<br /> <br /> This is bad.<br /> <br /> So, basically a moon god's scion is able to destroy a werewolf with silvery weapon<br /> <br /> A mage have nothing to do with a full dex-strenght scion that will bring him down in a sec<br /> <br /> So... scions are the strongest?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rules flat out state that using level 11 Boons and Epic Attributes gives you narrative control of the situation. Basically, you usurp the Story Teller for the the purpose of anything regarding that purview / attribute. For example, you could use level 11 Epic Strength to throw planets with one hand, or level 11 Epic Stamina to regenerate from a dust particle!<br /> <br /> So yeah, an in game mechanic that lets you hijack the story, I'd say they're pretty god damn powerful! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-19-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:26:53-08:00","id":1168863,"title":"","content":"I miss this from the old forums. When your high end character is a literal god though it's a bit one sided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:40:51-08:00","id":1168865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1168863#post1168863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss this from the old forums. When your high end character is a literal god though it's a bit one sided.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, though, Scion 1E considers Vampires and Werecritters to be Demigod level threats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:33:24-08:00","id":1168903,"title":"","content":"Apples to Oranges to Nukes. The power level has always been W/CoD &gt; Scion &gt; Nobilis, at least when talking about your average character that actually gets played. And to be fair to World/Chronicles of Darkness, the setting can actually go really high, with horrible elder gods when you peek behind the curtain to see what lies in the realms beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-21-2017, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:11:10-08:00","id":1168954,"title":"","content":"Oh, are we playing the \u201clet\u2019s downplay one gameline\u2019s characters in favor of another, purely based on the latter\u2019s setting with no regards to actually integrate the settings, or take anything other than raw power into account\u201d game again?<br /> <br /> Kratos kills every God, and Scions are nothing but warm-up to him. End of the game. <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, just as there\u2019s nothing stopping Scion players from declaring their characters true divinity, there\u2019s nothing stopping WoD/CofD players from declaring the Gods and their Scions are mere Umbrood/Goetia. This is ultimately a matter of which setting you wish to prioritize at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:18:46-08:00","id":1168955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1168903#post1168903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apples to Oranges to Nukes. The power level has always been W/CoD &gt; Scion &gt; Nobilis, at least when talking about your average character that actually gets played. And to be fair to World/Chronicles of Darkness, the setting can actually go really high, with horrible elder gods when you peek behind the curtain to see what lies in the realms beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to disagree with that assessment. In most Darkness games, the scenario goes <i>&quot;Oh shit, eldritch abomination, we need to run!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> While as in Scion, it's <i>&quot;Oh shit, eldritch abomination. I'm going to turn it into a pair of boots!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to the Darkness setting, the national level threats are extremely rare individuals who most players never get the chance to play from their perspective.<br /> <br /> But in Scion, national level threats are par for the course after your first chronicle, or so. And you even get to stand against them as an equal, instead of a hopeless underdog. By the time you hit Demigod status (which only requires Legend 4, by the way), your adventures graduate to inter-dimensional scale when you're traveling to and from pocket realities, or even taking a trip to the Underworld itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-19-2017, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T20:52:08-08:00","id":1169004,"title":"","content":"This is a bit like asking, &quot;is my character from &quot;Monsters and other childish things&quot; weaker than your PC from &quot;Godlike&quot;? There isn't any comparison. Can deities overpower semi-mortal monsters? Well, if they can't, there's something wrong with the deities. Was there a purpose to asking the question in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T23:54:05-08:00","id":1169022,"title":"","content":"Well masquerade vs fallen were always fun to read, especially when it got into the fluff theology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T00:56:49-08:00","id":1169028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169004#post1169004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit like asking, &quot;is my character from &quot;Monsters and other childish things&quot; weaker than your PC from &quot;Godlike&quot;? There isn't any comparison. Can deities overpower semi-mortal monsters? Well, if they can't, there's something wrong with the deities. Was there a purpose to asking the question in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Granted that there are some monsters (such as Vampires) in Scion who can increase their Legend rating by eating / sacrificing the Scions.<br /> <br /> So it is <i>technically possible</i> for the monsters to hold their own against them. But they would have to start small and work their way up to the big leagues.<br /> <br /> And as I said, werewolves and vampires are first presented as threats in the Demigod book, rather than showing up around the Hero level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-20-2017, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T03:41:07-08:00","id":1169042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1168954#post1168954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, are we playing the \u201clet\u2019s downplay one gameline\u2019s characters in favor of another, purely based on the latter\u2019s setting with no regards to actually integrate the settings, or take anything other than raw power into account\u201d game again?<br /> <br /> Kratos kills every God, and Scions are nothing but warm-up to him. End of the game. <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, just as there\u2019s nothing stopping Scion players from declaring their characters true divinity, there\u2019s nothing stopping WoD/CofD players from declaring the Gods and their Scions are mere Umbrood/Goetia. This is ultimately a matter of which setting you wish to prioritize at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this question is mostly pointless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but a slight pedantic point... As a son of Zeus, Kratos IS a Scion... In fact one whose traditional Hero to God development has been interfered with (and arguably accelerated) by Gods and Titans and Primordials at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T04:29:28-08:00","id":1169046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169042#post1169042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that this question is mostly pointless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but a slight pedantic point... As a son of Zeus, Kratos IS a Scion... In fact one whose traditional Hero to God development has been interfered with (and arguably accelerated) by Gods and Titans and Primordials at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that crossed my mind, like, two seconds after I pressed Post Reply - hardly the first time I compromised my own arguments : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T10:50:49-08:00","id":1169135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169042#post1169042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that this question is mostly pointless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but a slight pedantic point... As a son of Zeus, Kratos IS a Scion... In fact one whose traditional Hero to God development has been interfered with (and arguably accelerated) by Gods and Titans and Primordials at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was confused after the second game as to what Kratos was supposed to be. The first game ends with him becoming God of War, but in the second game, Zeus tricks him into sealing all his godly power into the Sword of Olympus, and turning him mortal. Yet he still has enough strength and power to tear Olympus to shreds?<br /> <br /> On a side note, he didn't kill Aphrodite, which means the goddess of love is still out there in the world. I'm curious what would have happened to Greece if she died and 'love' was allowed to run wild throughout the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-20-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T11:05:36-08:00","id":1169142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169135#post1169135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was confused after the second game as to what Kratos was supposed to be. The first game ends with him becoming God of War, but in the second game, Zeus tricks him into sealing all his godly power into the Sword of Olympus, and turning him mortal. Yet he still has enough strength and power to tear Olympus to shreds?<br /> <br /> On a side note, he didn't kill Aphrodite, which means the goddess of love is still out there in the world. I'm curious what would have happened to Greece if she died and 'love' was allowed to run wild throughout the land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I figure that after Zeus depowered him, Gaia Chose him as a Scion of Titans/Primordials or some such and he basically rebuilt his Legend all the way back up. It's not a clean fit into the system.<br /> <br /> He didn't kill Artemis either, by the way (not taking into consideration all the Gods who don't actually appear in the game, like Apollo or Demeter or Dionysus... though IIRC both of the last two got parts of themselves grafted onto Hera of all people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T12:05:16-08:00","id":1169165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169142#post1169142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I figure that after Zeus depowered him, Gaia Chose him as a Scion of Titans/Primordials or some such and he basically rebuilt his Legend all the way back up. It's not a clean fit into the system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, he escapes from the Underworld several times over the course of the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T19:29:21-08:00","id":1169256,"title":"","content":"I never played OWOD hunter, but couldn't they negate a supernaturals powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T22:59:07-08:00","id":1169274,"title":"","content":"Stop being mean, y'all. If we can't have arguments like &quot;could goku beat superman&quot; on the Internet, why do we even have the Internet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T01:56:53-08:00","id":1169293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169256#post1169256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never played OWOD hunter, but couldn't they negate a supernaturals powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, of course, just one of those points where comparison just can't be done fairly.<br /> <br /> Reckoning Hunters have a few powers that let them mess with a &quot;monster's&quot; powers. In the WoD, the presumption is that anything supernatural (besides other Imbued) was a &quot;monster&quot; in this context. Should a Scion be a monster though? Scions aren't from a setting with the same metaphysical assumptions about what is and isn't a valid monster to a Hunter's Edges.<br /> <br /> And, of course, how you choose to translate the systems matters a lot. This is even a problem in WoD to WoD crossover games. Reckoning had monster building rules in it so you don't have to buy the other core books just to make antagonists, and those rules presumed 99% of monster powers required them to spend points to activate. So many of the (few) Edges that directly interfere with supernatural powers tend to target the ability to spend points rather than blanket shutting down of things (which also means you avoid things like, 'is a vampire simply walking around a supernatural power I can disrupt?'). Being able to stop a Scion from spending Legend points at all, and Willpower to activate Boons/Knacks, could let an Imbued stymie Scions in pretty surprising ways, but it's not going to stop Epic physicals from simply crushing them to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T03:35:24-08:00","id":1169304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169293#post1169293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reckoning Hunters have a few powers that let them mess with a &amp;quot;monster's&amp;quot; powers. In the WoD, the presumption is that anything supernatural (besides other Imbued) was a &amp;quot;monster&amp;quot; in this context. Should a Scion be a monster though? Scions aren't from a setting with the same metaphysical assumptions about what is and isn't a valid monster to a Hunter's Edges.<br /> <br /> And, of course, how you choose to translate the systems matters a lot. This is even a problem in WoD to WoD crossover games. Reckoning had monster building rules in it so you don't have to buy the other core books just to make antagonists, and those rules presumed 99% of monster powers required them to spend points to activate. So many of the (few) Edges that directly interfere with supernatural powers tend to target the ability to spend points rather than blanket shutting down of things (which also means you avoid things like, 'is a vampire simply walking around a supernatural power I can disrupt?'). Being able to stop a Scion from spending Legend points at all, and Willpower to activate Boons/Knacks, could let an Imbued stymie Scions in pretty surprising ways, but it's not going to stop Epic physicals from simply crushing them to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually sounds like a good idea as a scion antagonist to me, have imbued organise and give them knowledge of fatebinding. The mortal resistance against the false gods/demon spawn. Could make a good story when fighting titans gets dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T08:37:16-08:00","id":1169363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1168955#post1168955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree with that assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what part of your post is a disagreement. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-21-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T10:33:21-08:00","id":1169402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169363#post1169363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what part of your post is a disagreement. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You used:W/COD &gt; Scion &gt; Nobilis to describe their power scale.<br /> <br /> Now it's been a while, but I'm pretty sure the &gt; symbol is supposed to face towards the greater number.<br /> <br /> Oh... wait, are those supposed to be arrows? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T11:53:41-08:00","id":1169433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169402#post1169402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh... wait, are those supposed to be arrows? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are supposed to be arrows. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T12:11:55-08:00","id":1169438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169433#post1169433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are supposed to be arrows. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry! I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> Also, what's Nobilis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T13:22:52-08:00","id":1169456,"title":"","content":"Nobilis is an RPG about playing avatars of greater beings that created you to manage specific affairs while they deal with much bigger problems out in the wider mythic universe. The PCs are obviously not the most powerful beings for it, but their control over the specific aspects of their creators starts somewhere around low level deity level in Scion terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T13:40:52-08:00","id":1169459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169456#post1169456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobilis is an RPG about playing avatars of greater beings that created you to manage specific affairs while they deal with much bigger problems out in the wider mythic universe. The PCs are obviously not the most powerful beings for it, but their control over the specific aspects of their creators starts somewhere around low level deity level in Scion terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand, the 'specific aspect' you have control over is one of the fundamental concepts underpinning the world, which can include such things as Waves, Borders, Strength, Eternity, Blankets, Caves, Conspiracy, Pride, Persuasion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T13:52:39-08:00","id":1169464,"title":"","content":"also at least one of the additions had a weird ass diceless system, I played a immortal sword duelist, transfigured into a teddy bear, with control over the concept of single combat, it is a strange game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T13:57:38-08:00","id":1169465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169456#post1169456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobilis is an RPG about playing avatars of greater beings that created you to manage specific affairs while they deal with much bigger problems out in the wider mythic universe. The PCs are obviously not the most powerful beings for it, but their control over the specific aspects of their creators starts somewhere around low level deity level in Scion terms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, right, that actually sounds familiar now. In fact, I think </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V3RNnL715tM\" target=\"_blank\">Puffin Forest</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> did a video talking about the game.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:54:48-08:00","id":1169540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169459#post1169459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To expand, the 'specific aspect' you have control over is one of the fundamental concepts underpinning the world, which can include such things as Waves, Borders, Strength, Eternity, Blankets, Caves, Conspiracy, Pride, Persuasion...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also things like: Ramen noodles, You know your a 90s kid if articles, and incombustiblity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T22:06:06-08:00","id":1169574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169464#post1169464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also at least one of the additions had a weird ass diceless system, I played a immortal sword duelist, transfigured into a teddy bear, with control over the concept of single combat, it is a strange game.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the editions're diceless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T02:14:39-08:00","id":1171753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1169465#post1169465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, right, that actually sounds familiar now. In fact, I think </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V3RNnL715tM\" target=\"_blank\">Puffin Forest</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> did a video talking about the game.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that's Nobilis. It's.. not a very good video (for one thing, he's reading something with a clearly whimsical tone as incredibly self-serious and giving the game flak because of that, and for another he keeps skipping over the parts of the game that tell you what it's about and then insisting that the game doesn't tell you what it's about), but that's Nobilis.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, <i>every</i> edition of Nobilis is diceless, yes. Nobilis is partially famous as &quot;that one game with no dice&quot; and partially famous as &quot;that weird high-powered storygame nobody actually plays (or understands how to play).&quot;<br /> <br /> And the occasional argument over whether Nobilis or Exalted is higher-powered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T03:42:12-08:00","id":1171760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1171753#post1171753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, that's Nobilis. It's.. not a very good video (for one thing, he's reading something with a clearly whimsical tone as incredibly self-serious and giving the game flak because of that, and for another he keeps skipping over the parts of the game that tell you what it's about and then insisting that the game doesn't tell you what it's about), but that's Nobilis.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, <i>every</i> edition of Nobilis is diceless, yes. Nobilis is partially famous as &quot;that one game with no dice&quot; and partially famous as &quot;that weird high-powered storygame nobody actually plays (or understands how to play).&quot;<br /> <br /> And the occasional argument over whether Nobilis or Exalted is higher-powered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I hear &quot;diceless sysem&quot; I think of a sandbox narrative where the players use their imagination (instead of hard mechanics) to act out the story.<br /> <br /> It's difficult to get used to, especially if you've got players who want their character to be successful as much as possible. But once you do get used to it, it can be pretty fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:50:16-08:00","id":1171880,"title":"","content":"Nobilis actually does have mechanics! They're just resource-based rather than randomness-based. If you want to make sure you beat the other guy in a contest, you need to invest enough resources until your numbers are higher than his numbers (instead of rolling dice and hoping your numbers end up higher than his numbers), but then you've lost those resources for the rest of the Story.<br /> <br /> It makes for a very different paradigm, but it's an interesting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T14:57:57-08:00","id":1171896,"title":"","content":"It would be very surprising if Nobilis was a rules lite game when it's latest edition's core is a 370 page rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T17:11:44-08:00","id":1171920,"title":"","content":"The font is large, there's a lot of whitespace surrounding the text, and there's a good number of full-page art splashes and the like, but I wouldn't call it strictly rules-lite, no.<br /> <br /> Compared to something like Exalted or 3.5e D&amp;D it would be, but it's got rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T20:16:40-08:00","id":1172501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1171753#post1171753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the occasional argument over whether Nobilis or Exalted is higher-powered.</div> </div> </div> </div>There used to be arguments about Scion vs Exalted way back when, and the end result is usually the same as arguments between Nobilis vs Exalted. The Exalt stands in a tiny bubble of perfect defense while the Scion / Noble gets bored and goes on with their adventures. =D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:37:31-08:00","id":1172547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1168734-are-the-scions-the-strongest?p=1172501#post1172501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There used to be arguments about Scion vs Exalted way back when, and the end result is usually the same as arguments between Nobilis vs Exalted. The Exalt stands in a tiny bubble of perfect defense while the Scion / Noble gets bored and goes on with their adventures. =D</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that used to be the end result. 3e steps away from that, 'cause like you say, that sort of thing renders combat null.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}